              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "LITTLEHOSS"
            },
            "reviewBody": "There is a similar recipe which I prefer called \"Hot Jezebel\". Take a jar of orange marmalade and mix in some horseradish to taste over low heat. Our the mixture over the cream cheese and spread on bread or crackers. Good stuff!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "bankermom24"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I love this appetizer! I make my own pepper jelly and mold the cream cheese in a small round dish or make a log out of it so it doesn't look like a brick of cheese :) Just line the dish with saran wrap - soften the cheese and press it into the dish. Chill until firm and then turn it out onto your serving platter.",
            "datePublished": "2011-11-04T14:35:32.737Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ARNOLDIRR"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is really yummy. I made a plate of appetizers for a party by spreading a little cream cheese on top of snack crackers then a little blop of jalapeno jelly on top of each one. I brought home an empty plate. Quick and easy but oh so good.",
            "datePublished": "2003-05-26T09:15:49.967Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "WOLFECOOKIE"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This stuff is awesome! I crave it! My dad had it at my son's birthday party and stated that it \"would taste great on a roof tile\". My favorite type of jelly to use (if you can find it) is raspberry chipotle jelly - YUM!!!!",
            "datePublished": "2003-03-30T12:15:40.903Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "mle"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I've made this twice. Each time I used different kinds of jalepeno pepper jelly, and it was gobbled up - people couldn't get enough. I now keep a jar of pepper jelly and the cream cheese on hand for a quick appetizer for surprise company.",
            "datePublished": "2008-09-14T16:22:36.910Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "JENNSCOOKIN"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I love this appetizer. It is definitely addictive.\r\nI tried it the first time at a church event. It was made with homemade jelly. I went to a party and tried it again. I asked the hostess how to make it. She said you just buy a jar of pepper jelly and pour it over the cream cheese. I drove straight to the grocery store to buy the pepper jelly and ate it for a snack. Yummy. I love to eat this with Ritz crackers, but you could also use tortillas chips.",
            "datePublished": "2003-11-24T13:34:55.263Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "i never measure"
            },
            "reviewBody": "this is a really good appetizer. my girlfriend made this for me not too long ago and we loved it....she used the hot pepper jelly but both are good.. ..",
            "datePublished": "2008-10-24T05:53:55.040Z"
          },
          {
